  "title": "Byju's: NCLAT dismisses appeals by BCCI, Riju Raveendran against NCLT order",
  "publication_date": "2023-03-18T10:39:02Z",
  "summary": "The National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT) has dismissed appeals filed by the Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) and Riju Raveendran challenging a National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) order regarding Byju's settlement.",
  "content": "The National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT) has rejected appeals filed by the Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) and Riju Raveendran against an NCLT order concerning Byju's settlement terms. The case relates to ongoing legal proceedings involving the prominent edtech company Byju's.\n\nThe NCLT had previously issued an order regarding settlement terms, which was subsequently challenged by both the BCCI and Raveendran. However, the NCLAT has now upheld the original NCLT decision by dismissing these appeals.",
